WEBVTT

00:00:00.367 --> 00:00:02.767
Who checks the checker?

00:00:04.367 --> 00:00:06.927
Step one: your answer comes first.

00:00:07.307 --> 00:00:11.827
It's saved — with the question and the task — before any review begins.

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:16.880
Step two: an independent judge checks it against the rubric.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:22.400
Step three: the result lands beside your work, with a reason you can open.

00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:25.400
If the review missed something, flag it.

00:00:25.933 --> 00:00:32.153
Judgements also decide what you practise next — tuned on two hundred and eighty-eight practice states.

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:35.520
A second opinion — not the final word.

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:38.100
Keating: judgement you can check.
